<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Layout xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>true</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>true</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Investor Information</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Required</behavior>
                <field>Name</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Required</behavior>
                <field>Phone</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Required</behavior>
                <field>LeadSource</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <!-- Status is NOT one of the 7 requested fields, but Salesforce rejects any Lead
                 layout that omits it: Lead.Status is a database-required standard field (see
                 the memory-recorded live-describe finding: nillable=false, independently of
                 FLS/permissionable) and a check-only dry-run validate against this org failed
                 with "Layout must contain an item for required layout field: Status" until this
                 item was added back. Placed last in this column so it disturbs the requested
                 field order as little as possible.
                 Behavior is Required, not Readonly: a check-only dry-run deploy of this layout
                 against DPEG-IR-Implementation on 2026-08-15 (both alone and paired with the
                 Investor Onboarding record page) FAILED with "[Layout] Lead-Investor Onboarding
                 Layout :: Field:Status must not be Readonly" ; the platform rejects Readonly on
                 a database-required standard field outright, regardless of any default value
                 supplied by a business process.
                 Preventing hand-edits to Status day-to-day is an OPEN QUESTION, not a solved
                 one ; do not assume this Required setting alone keeps it safe. A Dynamic Forms
                 conversion of the record page (omitting Status from the field body entirely)
                 was attempted on 2026-08-15 specifically to close that gap and was rejected by
                 the platform (see agent memory for the full investigation) ; the record page
                 has been reverted to its original force:detailPanel / page-layout-driven shape.
                 The standard "Edit" record action reads its field list from THIS layout
                 regardless of what the record page displays, and this layout lists Status as
                 Required (i.e. editable) ; that Edit modal remains a live path to hand-edit
                 Status today. Field-level permission (FLS) is the only mechanism identified so
                 far that would actually prevent a hand-edit ; it has not yet been applied.
                 Status is still expected to move primarily via the Under Review / Create
                 Profile quick actions, but that is a UX convention here, not an enforced
                 restriction. This layout-level Required setting exists only to satisfy the
                 platform's own layout-validation rule, not to express an access decision. -->
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Required</behavior>
                <field>Status</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Required</behavior>
                <field>Email</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Is_Accredited__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>true</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>true</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Additional Details</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Referred_By__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Description</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
